`POST /order/orders/{order_id}/send_update_billing_email` emails the customer a link to update their billing information
on an order that is in Accounts Receivable.  It is the API version of the "Send Billing Update" button on the Accounts
Receivable Process Payment screen.  The email goes out within a minute.

While the order is less than 7 days old, UltraCart sends a reminder every 2 days after this email.

The call is refused with HTTP 400 when:
- the order is not in Accounts Receivable
- the order does not have a valid email address
- the update billing email is turned off for the account
- a StoreFront communication flow handles unprocessed payments for the order (the flow emails the customer instead)
- this method already sent the email for the order in the last 24 hours

Requires SDK 4.1.260 or later when called through an SDK.

**Request \[[Create API Key](https://ultracart.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ucdoc/pages/38688545/API+Simple+Key)\]**
```bash
curl -X POST "https://secure.ultracart.com/rest/v2/order/orders/DEMO-0009104436/send_update_billing_email" \
  -H "Accept: application/json" \
  -H "X-UltraCart-Api-Version: 2017-03-01" \
  -H "x-ultracart-simple-key: 55f7c4940f843d01a10c5d77f17001009dcc02345e79bd01a10c5d77f1700100"
```

**Response Body**
```json
{
    "success": true,
    "metadata": {}
}
```

**Error Response Body** (HTTP 400)
```json
{
    "error": {
        "developer_message": "The update billing email was already sent for this order through the API in the last 24 hours.",
        "user_message": "The update billing email was already sent for this order through the API in the last 24 hours."
    },
    "success": false
}
```
